# Parameterized ADT alias: [type [let a] [Ok a] [Error String]] must register with
# one type parameter, enabling correct instantiation at each use site.
# Both constructors are injected: Ok (polymorphic on a) and Error (takes String).
# At runtime: constructors appear in the type dict as callable functions.
[
  Result: [type [let a] [Ok a] [Error String]]
  v1: [Ok 99]
  v2: [Error "oops"]
]
=== out
Dict({"Result": Dict({"Ok": Function(), "Error": Function()}), "v1": Variant(Result.Ok, Int(99)), "v2": Variant(Result.Error, String("oops"))})
